-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  dir_addresdata.pcpp - Directive compliance: @addresdata

  @addresdata "<key>" "<path>"; builds the file at <path> into the program
  under <key>, the same on every target (BNF.md sec 2). Any module may give
  it, as many times as it needs. The key is text, read as written; the path
  resolves once, as every path directive ($P: = the folder pcpp.exe is in).
  dir_addresdata_hello.txt beside this file is the data it adds.

  How to check, from repo\bin:
    pcpp res\tests\dir_addresdata.pcpp
    pcpp res\tests\dir_addresdata.pcpp -t x86_64-linux-gnu
  Nothing is reported.

  Break it: run each file below the same way; each reports exactly what the
  // comment on its marked line says, and nothing else:
    dir_addresdata_err_shape.pcpp       the path after the key is missing
    dir_addresdata_err_nofile.pcpp      the path names no existing file
    dir_addresdata_err_key.pcpp         the key is empty
    dir_addresdata_err_reserved.pcpp    the key starts with pcpp/ (the compiler's)
    dir_addresdata_err_duplicate.pcpp   a key an imported unit already adds
    dir_addresdata_err_duplicate_lib.pcpp   a key a separately built library adds too
                                        (linked: dir_addresdata_err_duplicate_lib_dep.pcpp)
*******************************************************************************/

module exe dir_addresdata;
@addresdata "hello" "$P:res/tests/dir_addresdata_hello.txt";
@addresdata "texts/hello again" "$P:res/tests/dir_addresdata_hello.txt";

begin
end.
